{
 "_provenance": "RE-MEASURED 2026-08-23 from GitHub-hosted ubuntu-latest CI logs (TEST-SPEED-01 lever 1). Weights are per-module wall seconds printed by scripts/shard_tests.py's own 'MODULE PASS ... seconds=' line, harvested from every ordinary shard job of runs 32621080380 and 32609926884 (python 3.11 and 3.14, four observations per module). Each weight is the MAXIMUM observation across both runs and both interpreters, because shard packing must not underestimate the binding interpreter (3.11 is consistently the slower one). Superseded map: quiet-bench serial timings of 2026-08-03, which covered 93 of the 140 modules and understated the hosted cost of the heavy tail by up to 68x (tests.test_whole_window_selection 7.292 s bench vs 498.9 s hosted; tests.test_reduce 48.386 s vs 1544.5 s). That understatement is what produced the observed 41-minute shard-3 job against a 175-second estimate. Bench numbers are NOT interchangeable with hosted numbers for this purpose and the bench corpus is retained separately under docs/process_traces/2026-08-23-speed/ rather than in this scheduling map.",
 "unknown_module_weight_seconds": 29.834,
 "_unknown_module_weight_rationale": "Arithmetic MEAN of the measured hosted weights, used by scripts/shard_tests.py's conservative_unknown_weight() for a module that is discovered but not yet measured. The historical fallback was the MEDIAN (0.868 s); on a distribution this heavy-tailed the median asserts that an unmeasured module is free, so a newly added heavy module is packed into an already-full shard and the job overruns silently. The mean reserves the cost of an average module instead. default_module_weight() retains median semantics because tests/test_shard_tests.py pins them.",
 "_zero_observation_floor": "2 modules completed faster than the runner's millisecond print resolution and were recorded as 0.000 s; they are floored to 0.001 s because load_timing_map() requires a strictly positive weight. The floor is scheduling-irrelevant (these modules are ~0% of a 4117-second suite). Floored: tests.test_audit_clock, tests.test_audit_report",
